---
name: upgrade-sc-compose
version: 3.0.0
description: Unattended sc-compose upgrade - edit the repo pin, handle the changelog, test old against new, PR, and release when nothing else is in flight.
format: toml
required_variables:
  - parent
  - ref
  - phase
  - from_version
  - to_version
  - priority
---
{#
sc-compose beads formula (sc-compose/beads/v1). Poured ids are
<parent>.<ref>-<step>.

Run (the lead, no input from Rand):
1. from_version = SC_COMPOSE_WHEEL_PIN in .claude/lib/sc_compose_dependency.py
   on develop; to_version = the sc-compose release to adopt; phase = the next
   free phase letter; parent = lint-phase-<phase>; ref = "upgrade".
2. Create the root (plan-root.json.j2, integration_branch
   integrate/phase-<phase>), cut and push integrate/phase-<phase> from develop,
   and commit to it .atm-bd/phase-<phase>.toml (plan
   docs/plans/phase-<phase>.jsonl, the root, the branch) and the plan file,
   one line: {"sprint": "phase-<phase>.upgrade-sprint"}.
3. `sc-compose bead attach` this formula under the root, then
   `.claude/skills/atm-beads/scripts/validate-plan --phase <phase>`.
4. `bd create --id <parent>-plan-qa --type task -l phase-<phase>,stage:plan-review
   --title "phase-<phase>: plan review"`, `bd update <parent>-plan-qa --parent
   <parent>`, `bd dep add <parent>.<ref>-sprint <parent>-plan-qa` and
   `bd dep add <parent>.<ref>-upgrade <parent>-plan-qa`, then close it
   with reason "formula plan-reviewed in phase-j at <commit of this formula on
   develop>". This is the one QA gate the lead closes: the formula is the plan
   and is not re-reviewed per run.
5. Execute only the poured steps, in needs order, through
   atm-bd-orchestration. A run plans no new steps.
6. After the last poured bead closes, close the sprint container and the root
   (reason "complete", or "not planned: BREAKING"), and delete
   integrate/phase-<phase> once Rand has merged its PR to develop.

Every stop the kit would report to the user (validate-plan problems, bd sync
failures, SANITY.ROUND_CAP) and every decision and escalation goes to
omega-prime@hermes with `atm send omega-prime@hermes --stdin <<'EOF'`. The
only waits on Rand are his merges of the PRs to develop and main; no agent
merges to develop or main.

The version constants changed are SC_COMPOSE_WHEEL_PIN and the minimum floors
in the upgrade step's deliverable 1; the kit-owned-file rule is in its
deliverable 2. `sc-compose bead` exits 0 on refusal; read
payload.outcome, never the exit code.
#}
formula = "upgrade-sc-compose"
description = "Upgrade sc-compose {{{ from_version }}} -> {{{ to_version }}} (phase-{{{ phase }}})."
version = 3
type = "workflow"

[[steps]]
id = "sprint"
title = "phase-{{{ phase }}}: sprint {{{ phase }}}-1 sc-compose {{{ to_version }}}"
description = "Sprint container for the sc-compose {{{ to_version }}} upgrade; QA fix groups attach under it. The run executes only the steps poured from this formula, in needs order, and plans no new steps. Container only: do not dispatch it. The lead closes it after {{{ parent }}}.{{{ ref }}}-qa and every fix group under it close."
type = "task"
priority = {{{ priority }}}
labels = ["phase-{{{ phase }}}", "stack:phase-{{{ phase }}}", "stage:sprint"]

[steps.metadata]
phase = "{{{ phase }}}"
sprint = "{{{ phase }}}-1"
stack = "phase-{{{ phase }}}"
layer = 1
difficulty = "fast"
pr_target = "integrate/phase-{{{ phase }}}"
requirements = ["REQ-PRODUCT-025", "REQ-PRODUCT-026", "REQ-PRODUCT-027", "REQ-PRODUCT-028", "REQ-PRODUCT-029", "REQ-PRODUCT-030", "REQ-PRODUCT-031"]
adrs = ["NONE"]

[[steps]]
id = "upgrade"
title = "phase-{{{ phase }}}: pin sc-compose {{{ to_version }}}"
description = """
## Deliverables
1. `.claude/lib/sc_compose_dependency.py`: `SC_COMPOSE_WHEEL_PIN` reads {{{ to_version }}}, and the floors `MIN_SC_COMPOSE`, `MIN_SC_COMPOSE_TEXT`, `MIN_SC_COMPOSE_BINDING`, `MIN_SC_COMPOSE_BINDING_TEXT`, `SC_COMPOSE_INSTALL` and `SC_COMPOSE_BINDING_INSTALL` require {{{ to_version }}}.
2. Read randlee/sc-compose at tag v{{{ to_version }}}: every `CHANGELOG.md` section after {{{ from_version }}} up to {{{ to_version }}}, `docs/migration-notes.md` and `docs/migration/`. List each breaking change, deprecation and recommended change in this bead's notes. For each one, `git grep` the repo for the affected command, flag, API or template syntax and either (a) apply it to the repo-owned use, append the path to this bead's `owned_paths` before editing it, and name the changelog item and grep in the notes, or (b) record "not used" with the grep. A use in a kit- or other-skill-owned file is not edited: file a GitHub issue against the owning repo, link it in the notes, and `atm send omega-prime@hermes` the link. The diff holds only deliverable 1 and the (a) paths.
3. Two scratch environments: A = a worktree at this layer's base commit with sc-compose {{{ from_version }}}; B = this layer's head with sc-compose {{{ to_version }}}. Each gets the CLI from the randlee/sc-compose v<v> release asset (`gh release download v<v> -R randlee/sc-compose -p 'sc-compose_<v>_<target>.tar.gz'`, extracted into `<env>/bin`, first on PATH) and `<env>/venv/bin/pip install sc-compose==<v>`. Record `sc-compose --version` and the wheel version in each; a mismatch voids the run.
4. In A and in B, run `just lint`, `just test` and `python3 -m pytest -q .claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/scripts/tests .claude/skills/atm-beads/tests .claude/skills/triaging-findings/tests bindings/sc-lint-py/python/sc_lint/tests/test_orchestration_contracts.py`; record pass/fail per command and per failing test id.
5. In A and in B, from the worktree root, `mkdir -p target/upgrade-samples` and run `sc-compose bead validate --request <f> --json > target/upgrade-samples/<basename>.out.json` for each file in `.atm-bd/formula/upgrade-sc-compose.samples/`; each request's `rendered_formula` writes its rendered formula to `target/upgrade-samples/`. Record each payload.outcome, then `diff -r <A>/target/upgrade-samples <B>/target/upgrade-samples`.
6. Verdict. A break is anything passing in A that fails in B (deliverable 4), a sample outcome that differs, or a rendered formula that differs; a failure in both is pre-existing and reported, not a break. NOT_BREAKING: no break. A minor break is fixable in repo-owned files without changing a public interface, a kit- or other-skill-owned file, or the architecture: fix it in this layer as a deliverable 2(a) path and re-run deliverables 4-5 in B until it passes; when every break is minor and fixed, the verdict is BREAKING_FIXED, listing each break and its fix in the notes for the pr_develop step to announce in the PR to develop. Any other break is BREAKING: list each with its output or diff and why it needs architecture guidance. Record the verdict with `bd update <this bead> --set-metadata verdict=<NOT_BREAKING|BREAKING_FIXED|BREAKING>` and in the notes. BREAKING_FIXED and BREAKING complete this bead; they are not refusals.
7. A pin is an assignment or install spec of a version literal (`SC_COMPOSE_WHEEL_PIN = "x.y.z"`, `sc-compose==x.y.z`); imports, asserts and prose naming a constant are not pins. Outside `.github/scripts/` (sc-publish kit), the only repo-owned pin is deliverable 1; a new one is not edited: list it in the notes and `atm send omega-prime@hermes` the path for a planning change. Then `git grep -n "{{{ from_version }}}"` outside `docs/plans/`, `CHANGELOG.md` and `.github/scripts/`, and list each hit in the notes as descriptive or stale; a stale repo-owned doc naming {{{ from_version }}} references the sc-compose version and is a deliverable 2(a) path, a stale kit- or other-skill-owned doc follows the deliverable 2 issue path.

If the run cannot be done (tag or release asset missing, an environment will not install, a version mismatch), record the refusal in the notes, `atm send omega-prime@hermes` the reason, and leave this bead open.
"""
type = "task"
priority = {{{ priority }}}
labels = ["phase-{{{ phase }}}", "stack:phase-{{{ phase }}}", "stage:dev"]

[steps.metadata]
role = "dev"
phase = "{{{ phase }}}"
stack = "phase-{{{ phase }}}"
layer = 1
difficulty = "normal"
sprint = "{{{ phase }}}-1"
sprint_bead = "{{{ parent }}}.{{{ ref }}}-sprint"
branch = "sprint/{{{ phase }}}-1-sc-compose-{{{ to_version }}}"
pr_target = "integrate/phase-{{{ phase }}}"
owned_paths = [".claude/lib/sc_compose_dependency.py"]
requirements = ["REQ-PRODUCT-025", "REQ-PRODUCT-026", "REQ-PRODUCT-027", "REQ-PRODUCT-028", "REQ-PRODUCT-029", "REQ-PRODUCT-030", "REQ-PRODUCT-031"]
adrs = ["NONE"]

[[steps]]
id = "sanity"
title = "phase-{{{ phase }}}: sanity check"
description = """
## Deliverables
1. Sanity check of {{{ parent }}}.{{{ ref }}}-upgrade (required by atm-bd-orchestration before QA): each numbered deliverable is written and lint passes. This is not QA, and it needs no input from Rand.

Close on PASS only. On FAIL follow the kit's dev-fix round. A FAIL at the kit's round cap is an escalation: `atm send omega-prime@hermes` the failing deliverables.
"""
type = "task"
priority = {{{ priority }}}
labels = ["phase-{{{ phase }}}", "stack:phase-{{{ phase }}}", "stage:dev-sanity"]
needs = ["upgrade"]

[steps.metadata]
role = "dev-sanity"
phase = "{{{ phase }}}"
stack = "phase-{{{ phase }}}"
sprint = "{{{ phase }}}-1"
sprint_bead = "{{{ parent }}}.{{{ ref }}}-sprint"
dev_bead = "{{{ parent }}}.{{{ ref }}}-upgrade"
difficulty = "fast"

[[steps]]
id = "qa"
title = "phase-{{{ phase }}}: QA sc-compose {{{ to_version }}} pin"
description = """
## Deliverables
1. quality-mgr checks the upgrade bead's changelog list against the sc-compose CHANGELOG and migration docs (each item applied, not used, or issued), re-installs both versions, re-runs `just lint`, `just test` and the deliverable 4 pytest suites in A and B and records pass/fail per command, re-runs deliverables 5-6 with the same sample requests, and confirms the recorded versions, results, diffs and `metadata.verdict` match, and that each BREAKING_FIXED fix is minor (repo-owned, no public interface or architecture change). `git diff --name-only <base>...<head>` lists only `.claude/lib/sc_compose_dependency.py` (deliverable 1) and the `owned_paths` the notes justify. CI on the layer is green, or, only for BREAKING, red on the tests the verdict lists.

On FAIL, file the findings as fix groups under the sprint container per atm-bd-orchestration. After a second failed QA round, escalate with `atm send omega-prime@hermes` "sc-lint: sc-compose {{{ to_version }}} upgrade QA failed twice: <open findings>. <PR link>". Every escalation from this step is sent this way.
"""
type = "task"
priority = {{{ priority }}}
labels = ["phase-{{{ phase }}}", "stack:phase-{{{ phase }}}", "stage:qa"]
needs = ["sanity"]

[steps.metadata]
role = "qa"
phase = "{{{ phase }}}"
stack = "phase-{{{ phase }}}"
round = 1
difficulty = "normal"
sprint = "{{{ phase }}}-1"
sprint_bead = "{{{ parent }}}.{{{ ref }}}-sprint"
checked_bead = "{{{ parent }}}.{{{ ref }}}-upgrade"

[[steps]]
id = "pr_develop"
title = "phase-{{{ phase }}}: PR to develop"
description = """
The lead runs this step itself.

## Deliverables
1. After QA closed PASS and the layer PR's required checks are green, or red only on tests the verdict lists as breaking, merge the layer PR into integrate/phase-{{{ phase }}} (`gh pr merge <n> --merge`; a single layer is not a stack; the integration branch exists because validate-plan reads the plan file from it), open the ready integrate/phase-{{{ phase }}} -> develop PR, and request review from `rand-lee` (`gh api -X POST repos/randlee/sc-lint/pulls/<n>/requested_reviewers -f 'reviewers[]=rand-lee'`). Never merge it; only Rand merges to develop. Rand's merge is the only input this step waits for.
2. Decision point 1, on the upgrade bead's `metadata.verdict`. BREAKING_FIXED: when CI is green, the PR description announces each break and its fix as the impact assessment; close the release step with `bd close {{{ parent }}}.{{{ ref }}}-release --force --reason "not planned: BREAKING_FIXED"` and `atm send omega-prime@hermes` "sc-lint: sc-compose {{{ to_version }}} upgrade had minor breaking changes, fixed and listed in the PR; CI green. Rand, please complete <PR link>."; the run stops at this PR. BREAKING: the PR description carries an impact assessment: the verdict, each failing test and diff, and which repo uses of sc-compose they affect. Close the release step with `bd close {{{ parent }}}.{{{ ref }}}-release --force --reason "not planned: BREAKING"` and `atm send omega-prime@hermes` "sc-lint: sc-compose {{{ to_version }}} upgrade is BREAKING; the PR to develop is ready to merge with its impact assessment (CI red only on the listed breaking tests): <PR link>." with the failing tests; the run stops at this ready PR. Neither breaking verdict opens a PR to main. NOT BREAKING: when CI is green, `atm send omega-prime@hermes` "sc-lint: sc-compose {{{ to_version }}} upgrade, CI green. Rand, please complete <PR link>."; the run continues to the release step and its PR to main. If CI cannot go green, `atm send omega-prime@hermes` the failing check and leave this bead open.
3. Wait for Rand's merge: when omega-prime or Rand reports it, confirm with one REST read (`gh api repos/randlee/sc-lint/pulls/<n> --jq .merged`), then close this bead. No polling. This bead is open by design while it waits; the bead-queues cron and stall rules do not re-dispatch it.
"""
type = "task"
priority = {{{ priority }}}
labels = ["phase-{{{ phase }}}", "stack:phase-{{{ phase }}}", "stage:land"]
needs = ["qa", "sprint"]

[steps.metadata]
role = "lead"
phase = "{{{ phase }}}"

[[steps]]
id = "release"
title = "phase-{{{ phase }}}: patch release PR to main"
description = """
The lead dispatches this step to the publisher with `.claude/skills/publishing/preflight.xml.j2`; the publisher follows `.claude/skills/publishing/SKILL.md`.

Outcome: when no other work is in progress, the upgrade ends in a PR to main that carries a patch version bump and has passed publish-preflight, ready for Rand to merge.

## Deliverables
1. This step runs only on a NOT_BREAKING verdict (the upgrade bead's `metadata.verdict`); on any other value `atm send omega-prime@hermes` "sc-lint: sc-compose {{{ to_version }}} release step not run: verdict <verdict>.", close this bead and stop.
2. Decision point 2. Other work in progress = any open, in_progress or blocked bead labelled `phase-*` or `stage:release` whose id is neither {{{ parent }}} nor prefixed by `{{{ parent }}}.` (`bd list --status open,in_progress,blocked --json`), or an open PR to develop (`gh pr list --base develop --state open`). An open prior phase, planned or running, defers the release. If there is any, `atm send omega-prime@hermes` "sc-lint: sc-compose {{{ to_version }}} on develop; release deferred because <work>." and close this bead.
3. Otherwise bump the patch version (<next-patch> = the current version with the patch number plus one) on release/<next-patch>-prep; afterwards `git grep -n "<current version>"` outside `CHANGELOG.md` and `docs/plans/` finds no stale version string. Open the PR to develop with `rand-lee` as reviewer. When CI is green `atm send omega-prime@hermes` "sc-lint: <next-patch> version bump PR, CI green. Rand, please complete <PR link>.". When omega-prime or Rand reports the merge, confirm it with one REST read. This bead is open by design while it waits; no polling, and the cron does not re-dispatch it.
4. Dispatch `release-candidate.yml` from develop, run publish-preflight to GO, and open the develop -> main PR with `rand-lee` as reviewer. When CI is green `atm send omega-prime@hermes` "sc-lint: <version> release PR to main, preflight GO, CI green. Rand, please complete <PR link>.". If preflight or CI cannot go green, `atm send omega-prime@hermes` "sc-lint: <version> release blocked: <cause>. <link>" and leave this bead open. No agent merges to develop or main; Rand's merges are the only input this step waits for.
"""
type = "task"
priority = {{{ priority }}}
labels = ["phase-{{{ phase }}}", "stack:phase-{{{ phase }}}", "stage:release"]
needs = ["pr_develop"]

[steps.metadata]
role = "publisher"
phase = "{{{ phase }}}"
